---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import SignalChain from "../components/SignalChain.astro";
---
<Base title="Design" description="How Clessidra works: signal path, recording, density, grains, slices, level, with the firmware's values.">

<h1>Design</h1>
<p class="lead">How the firmware works. Every value is the firmware's.</p>

<h2 class="label" id="signal-path">Signal Path</h2>
<figure class="panel figure"><SignalChain /></figure>

<h2 class="label" id="record">Record</h2>
<div class="prose">
  <p>The input goes into a ring all the time. P10 takes from it into the buffer that isn't playing, then plays it. Grains playing finish on the old recording, new ones start on the new: no click, and no grain ever reads sound being written.</p>
</div>
<div class="panel table"><table>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Tap</td><td>Under 0.3 s: the 8 s before the touch</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Hold</td><td>From 50 ms before the touch to the release. Longer than 30 s keeps the last 30 s</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Trim</td><td>Silence below −60 dBFS cut at both ends, 5 ms kept. A silent recording changes nothing</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Landing</td><td>Copied at 21 times real time: 30 s in 1.4 s</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Selection</td><td>Length (S35) of the recording, placed by Position (S30) from its start to its end</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>

<h2 class="label" id="layers">Layers</h2>
<div class="panel table"><table>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Own</td><td>Each fader and knob: playhead, grain, mix</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Random</td><td>P11 held. S30 to S33: the randomness of position, size, shape and pitch</td></tr>
    <tr><td>FX</td><td>P00 held, over P11. S31 filter, S32 reverb</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Pick-up</td><td>A knob takes over a value only once it reaches it, so nothing jumps when a layer changes</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>

<h2 class="label" id="density">Density, Size, Shape, FX</h2>
<div class="panel table"><table>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Density</td><td>S37, as Beads. Off at the centre, periodic below, random above, 0.3 to 131 grains per second towards each end, exponential. A firm press on a slice raises its own</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Size</td><td>S31. 10 ms to 4 s, exponential, 200 ms at the centre, at most half the recording</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Shape</td><td>S32. Reverse percussive, Hann at the centre, percussive</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Filter</td><td>P00 + S31. Off at the centre. Low-pass down to 200 Hz, high-pass up to 2 kHz, resonance rising with it</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Reverb</td><td>P00 + S32. On the grains: amount up to equal parts, decay 0.5 to 16 s</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>
