<h2 class="label" id="grain">A Grain</h2>
<div class="panel table"><table>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Position</td><td>The playhead's point in the selection. Its randomness, P11 + S30: anywhere in what is playing</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Pitch</td><td>S33. Its randomness, P11 + S33: up to ±24 semitones</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Size</td><td>S31. Its randomness, P11 + S31: anywhere from 10 ms to 4 s</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Window</td><td>S32. Its randomness, P11 + S32: any shape</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Pan</td><td>Equal power, as Beads: the width grows with the grains sounding and with all the randomness, random starts included</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Randomness</td><td>As Beads' attenuverters. Off at the centre. Up: each grain moved by the amount towards a random value, an even spread. Down: by a random part of three times it, mostly near with a long tail</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Direction</td><td>The playhead's</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Duration</td><td>The same at any pitch</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>

<h2 class="label" id="starts">Starts and Voices</h2>
<div class="panel table"><table>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Starts</td><td>Grains per second, whatever their size. S37 as Beads: off at the centre, periodic below, random above: random intervals, without the closest starts and the longest gaps, at the same mean</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Voices</td><td>32. Over 24 sounding, the one furthest along fades out in 5 ms, so a new grain always starts</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Overlap</td><td>At high density the grains shorten, so 24 voices hold whole windows: 183 ms at 131 grains per second</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>

<h2 class="label" id="slices">Slices</h2>
<div class="prose">
  <p>Each new recording is cut into 7 slices at its onsets: a rise of 6 dB over the 30 ms before, in 5 ms frames, above −50 dBFS, at least 50 ms apart. The strongest onsets are kept, and each slice starts 5 ms before its onset. With too few onsets, the longest slices are halved.</p>
  <p>P03–P09 play the slices, first to last: left to right on the panel, top to bottom within a column. Each touch is its own stream of grains on top of the playhead, from the slice's start, at the playhead's speed and direction. Pressure sets its density, from a light touch to the most.</p>
</div>

<h2 class="label" id="speed">Playhead and Triggers</h2>
<div class="panel table"><table>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Speed</td><td>S36. 0 to 4 times, the square of the travel: 1 at the centre, with a detent. The bottom stops it, a tape stop</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Direction</td><td>S09. Up forward, down reverse. Centre freezes at once, and the speed comes back as it was</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Selection</td><td>The playhead goes round it</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Restart</td><td>P02. The playhead from the start of the selection</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Once</td><td>S07 up. A slice plays to its end. Frozen, it stops on release</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Gate</td><td>S07 centre. A slice plays while held</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Loop</td><td>S07 down. A slice goes round while held</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>

<h2 class="label" id="level">Level</h2>
<div class="panel table"><table>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Normaliser</td><td>Copies of one sound add up in amplitude, independent grains in power. Both are measured, smoothed over 5 ms, and the sum is brought back to the input's level with 0.9 headroom. Grains that cancel are not boosted</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Limiter</td><td>+6 dB in. Look-ahead 5 ms, ceiling −0.5 dBFS</td></tr>
    <tr><td>LED</td><td>Glows with the grains. A 300 ms pulse when a control reaches its centre. Steady while P11 or P00 is held: the value turned</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>

<h2 class="label" id="runtime">Runtime</h2>
<div class="panel table"><table>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Board</td><td>Daisy Seed. 48 kHz, 48-sample blocks (1 ms). Pads read every 3 ms</td></tr>
    <tr><td>CPU</td><td>v0.2.0: 16 % closed, 76 % at the heaviest settings, measured on the board. v0.3.0 to be measured</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Browser</td><td>The same code, compiled to WebAssembly. 48 kHz, 128-sample blocks, controls read once per block</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>
</Base>
